<title>INDIA: BSE figures of India carry forward trade-April 26.</title>
<headline>BSE figures of India carry forward trade-April 26.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the latest data, for the top 10 stocks by value, released by the Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) for the carry forward or &quot;badla&quot; account ended April 26</p>
<p>SCRIP		  SETTLEMENT  AV BADLA  QTY    VALUE   % BADLA</p>
<p>			 RATE				(RS MLN)</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>L&amp;T		    225	   0.59     164950   37.11   13.67</p>
<p>ACC		   1440	   3.80	20890   30.08   13.76</p>
<p>Castrol		435	   1.15	67550   29.38   13.78</p>
<p>Arvind Mills	 135	   0.37     149650   20.20   14.29</p>
<p>Bajaj Auto	   950	   2.53	21000   19.95   13.89</p>
<p>Tata Power	   136	   0.35     118650   16.14   13.42</p>
<p>State Bank	   315	   0.81	44770   14.10   13.41</p>
<p>Tata Steel	   182	   0.48	67710   12.32   13.75</p>
<p>Century Textiles  2075	   5.74	 5020   10.42   14.42</p>
<p>Tata Chem	    160	   0.41	61000    9.76   13.36</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The average badla charges work out to 13.36 percent on an annualised basis against 14.35 percent in the previous carry forward account ended April 19</p>
